id: pm-r97901
title: "GH-1174: Windows Node 24 receipt traversal negative control must fail closed portably"
description: "The nightly Windows gate exposes a platform-dependent receipt traversal fixture: replacing the tracker directory with a file produces invalid_evidence_count=0 on Windows while POSIX reports 1. Replace the host-sensitive setup with a deterministic cross-platform inaccessible/non-directory boundary, align SDK classification across operating systems, and retain a genuine negative control."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:merge","area:test",ci,"github:1174","platform:windows",regression
created_at: "2026-09-01T10:08:01.615Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-01T11:59:54.073Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-01T11:41:55.088Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-01T11:41:55.088Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: A deterministic cross-platform fixture reproduces an exact filesystem boundary error; the public SDK returns the same typed invalid reason and count on Windows and POSIX; focused Linux tests and a hosted Windows Node 24 run pass; the negative control still proves a known-bad path fails closed rather than weakening the assertion.
goal: project management = context management
objective: Restore portable fail-closed evidence verification
value: Nightly portability again detects product regressions instead of harness variance
impact: Restores the mandatory Windows gate and protects the SDK evidence contract across hosts
why_now: "The sole failure in 8,239 nightly tests is this receipt boundary regression."
parent: pm-dj98
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: "GitHub Actions windows-latest, Node 24, Vitest full nightly suite"
repro_steps: Run tests/unit/sdk/merge-receipts.spec.ts on windows-latest Node 24 at dd505d4; fails closed when a receipt directory path cannot be traversed expects invalid_evidence_count 1 and receives 0.
resolution: "Classify a missing receipt store by inspecting the exact requested path and then the nearest existing ancestor; only an existing directory proves absence, while files and inaccessible/I/O boundaries fail closed. Added real POSIX and injected Windows/error-path tests, exact first-coordinate assertions, SDK/CLI integration coverage, and merge-safety documentation."
expected_result: "The same non-directory or unreadable receipt-store topology is invalid evidence on Windows and POSIX, while genuinely absent directories remain empty evidence."
actual_result: "Hosted PR #1175 Windows regression Node 24 passed in 3m31s; focused tests passed 10/10 before review and the repository suite passed 8,244/8,244 with exact 100/100/100/100. Cubic exact-path feedback was incorporated before closure."
component: SDK merge-receipt file boundary and Windows test harness
