comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-01T10:08:01.615Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: exact GH-1174 search across all statuses returned zero. Historical Windows receipt items pm-v3umtp and pm-46hpx8 cover different path-shape defects; this failure is the newly shipped non-directory evidence control and therefore a distinct recurrence under the shared merge-evidence delivery."
  "2026-09-01T10:14:39.621Z","harness:codex","Root cause and fix: Windows reports an inner path below a file ancestor as ENOENT where POSIX reports ENOTDIR. Receipt discovery now walks to the nearest existing ancestor: a directory means a genuinely absent store, while a file or inaccessible ancestor is invalid evidence. The real filesystem negative control remains fail-closed and focused tests pass."
  "2026-09-01T11:14:28.813Z","harness:codex","Cross-platform evidence: receipt directory classification now walks to the nearest existing ancestor after a missing-path error. An existing directory proves an absent store; a file, permission failure, I/O failure, or other non-directory boundary remains invalid evidence. Real and dependency-injected filesystem tests cover POSIX ENOTDIR, Windows-style ENOENT, permission faults, filesystem-root termination, unreadable candidates, and bounded detail overflow."
  "2026-09-01T11:27:01.546Z","harness:codex","Local closure evidence is complete, including dependency-injected Windows-style ENOENT traversal and real POSIX filesystem cases. Item remains in progress only until the hosted Windows Node 24 job proves the original GH-1174 recurrence at the PR head; no other PM item is claimed or marked in progress for this delivery."
  "2026-09-01T11:41:53.579Z","harness:codex","Hosted Windows acceptance: PR #1175 Windows regression (Node 24) passed in 3m31s at head 1484629, directly proving the GH-1174 nightly recurrence. Cubic additionally caught the exact-path regular-file ENOENT boundary; the closeout fix starts inspection at the requested receipt path and the negative control asserts that first coordinate."
  "2026-09-01T11:59:54.073Z","harness:codex","Exact closeout evidence: a manual temporary Git repository replaced the durable receipt-store path itself with a regular file; the real built CLI returned ok=false, complete=false, invalid_evidence_count=1, evidence_source=durable, reason=directory_unreadable, and no truncation. Full static gates and exact coverage then passed; the nightly regression carries a runnable strengthened negative control."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-01T11:14:29.313Z","harness:codex",Windows can surface a missing descendant below a file ancestor as ENOENT where POSIX commonly reports ENOTDIR. Error-code equality is therefore insufficient; classify the nearest existing ancestor and fail closed unless it is a directory.
